-- title:
--   Digits in
-- statement:
--   **Digits in.** Stack `tX` holds `x < 2^{bM}`; afterwards `tX` is popped and stack `0` carries `gflat (digG b e M S x)` on top of its old contents.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFTDig`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFT.digI_spec (b e M S x : ℕ) (hx : x < 2 ^ (b * M)) (s : IState HS) (LX : List Item)
--       (hX : s.G tX = .int (x : ℤ) :: LX) :
--       IRuns I iprog (digI b e M S) s
--         ((s.upd tX LX).upd 0 (ints (gflat (digG b e M S x)) ++ s.G 0)) (cDig b e M S)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFT §1: digits in*: `digI b e M S`: with `x ≥ 0`, `x < 2^{bM}` on stack `tX`, it cuts the `M` radix-`2^b` digits
--   `a_j = ⌊x / 2^{bj}⌋ mod 2^b` off `x` (one `split` by the ruler `2^b` each, cost `O(b)`
--   independently of the size of the rest), and leaves on stack `0` the Gaussian array
--   `digG b e M S x = [(a_0 2^e, 0), …, (a_{M-1} 2^e, 0), (0,0), …]` of `S` entries (`gflat` form),
--   i.e. the scaled input coefficients `a_j 2^{p-b-2}` of §9.2.3 padded to `S` entries (`e = p-b-2`).
--   Cost `O(M (b + e + 1) + S + 1)`, all loop counters unary.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** This lemma belongs to the item-language (IL) layer of the integer-multiplication-kappa campaign: tape-level programs (register programs over 64 item stacks of the `NLogN` multitape framework, definition bundles `IntMul_HvdH_M_Defs1`–`IntMul_HvdH_M_Defs8`) that implement the data-movement primitives of the OpenAI preprint *Integer multiplication below $n\log n$* (field moves, row split/merge, shifts, the uniform Proposition 11 interchange, Lemma 12 with fine $O(1)$-per-element costs, Gaussian record primitives, Proposition 14 pieces) with exact list denotations from the array-model bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*` and explicit cost bounds. All names refer to the definition bundles up to `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs18`.
